Example builds
==============

From the repository root
```bash
make -C examples/grammar                          # Run grammar tests
make -C examples/farrow-lv sched                  # Schedule APS modules
make -C examples/bigger bigger-binding.sched      # or using .sched alias
make -C examples/farrow-lv scala EVALUATOR=STATIC # or manually specify evaluator
make -C examples scala                            # Build all Scala drivers
make -C examples test                             # Run configured tests
make -C examples/bigger BiggerBindingDriver.class # Build one driver
make -C examples/bigger BiggerBindingDriver.run ARGS=programs/bigger.program
```

Each folder contains one AST and its build configuration.

- `ast.mk`: names the folder's single AST source:

```Makefile
AST = tiny.aps
```

- `Makefile`: sets platform-independent parser inputs, scheduling, and test policy:

```Makefile
include ast.mk

LEXER / PARSER            .lex and .y input files, if the example has a parser
SCHED_MODULES             Modules to schedule (default: all .aps except AST)
TEST_DRIVERS              Drivers to test (default: all of the example's drivers)
TEST_PROGRAMS             Input globs, relative to the example folder (default: programs/*)

include ../common.mk
```

- `scala/scala.mk`: describes the example's Scala build:

```Makefile
DRIVERS                   Driver names, local to this example
DRIVER.<name>             <module>.aps <evaluators> <files.scala...> [MainObject]
SHARED_SOURCES            Additional APS or Scala inputs shared by the example's modules
MODULE_CONFIG             Rebuild dependencies (default: source folder's Makefile, scala/scala.mk, and ast.mk)
PARSER_BASENAME           Prefix for generated scanner, parser, and token classes
```
Example:

```Makefile
DRIVER.BiggerBindingDriver = bigger-binding.aps DYNAMIC,STATIC bigger-binding-driver.scala
DRIVER.SimpleBinding1Driver = simple-binding1.aps DYNAMIC,STATIC simple-binding-driver.scala SimpleBindingDriver
```
